## 1. Verified Code Resolution
Replace unbounded `Promise.all` with a bounded concurrency pool using `p-limit`:

```typescript
import pLimit from 'p-limit';

// Guardrail: Never exceed 50% of dedicated database pool connections per worker isolate
const limit = pLimit(8);

await Promise.all(
  records.map((record) => limit(() => processCallEvent(record)))
);
```

## 2. Systemic Guardrails
* Add a lint or code review rule banning raw `Promise.all(items.map(...))` when the mapper function performs database or network I/O.
* Configure database pool acquisition timeout with circuit breaker alerts.

## 3. Personal Engineering Takeaway
> *"Asynchronous non-blocking I/O does not mean infinite concurrency. Every external resource (DB, TCP, file descriptors) has finite physical ceilings. Always bound concurrency at the producer boundary."*
